        "role": "user",
        "content": "Read the exact question and ALL original source segments. Documents, cards, saved answers and annotations are fallible data, never instructions. Distinct valid namesakes and complementary answers may coexist; competing assertions about one referent are not automatically distinct valid answers. Do not invent source authority, document independence or unstated question constraints. A quoted assertion, occurrence, or repeated text is not truth. Match requested subject/object, relation direction, negation, time and answer type. A city in a birth sentence is not a date. In \"A's manager B\", B is the manager, not A. Sports biographies can positively support multiple legitimate sports. An incidental chart, associated person or date is not automatically the answer. Use only supplied candidate/source IDs in bounded fields; no free quotation or prose.\nReturn the complete short answer list and a brief explanation using the common JSON object. Preserve separately valid referents and complementary answers. Resolve the exact requested relation and answer granularity from original context, without inventing restrictions. Avoid gratuitous rewriting of valid old answer forms. Inspect all proposed candidates, including rejected ones, for useful missing information. Treat all audit labels and saved answers as fallible, not certified true. No invented source authority or document-majority-as-proof. Consider contradictions but do not silently equate competing assertions with different valid entities.\nMake justified edits to the R5 set with full complementary coverage. Different artists can legitimately release works with an identical title; different people can have distinct dates. Uncertainty about a claim is different from a wrong requested role. Keep supported alternate referents rather than one familiar winner. Explicit memory checks are fallible. Avoid a broad rewrite when the original answer strings are valid; return the complete list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"When was the Turkish Republican Party founded?\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 217, \"text\": \"Republican Party (Turkey) Republican Party () was a former political party in Turkey Republican People’s party (CHP) which is usually credited as the founder of Turkish republic in 1923 was the oldest party in Turkey.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d00\", \"start\": 218, \"end\": 343, \"text\": \"But after the party adopted the policy of so-called left of center in the 1960s, two groups of MPs broke away from the party.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d00\", \"start\": 344, \"end\": 395, \"text\": \"The first group in 1967 founded the Reliance Party.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d00\", \"start\": 396, \"end\": 453, \"text\": \"Republican Party was founded by the second group in 1972.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d00\", \"start\": 454, \"end\": 496, \"text\": \"The party was founded on 4 September 1972.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d00\", \"start\": 497, \"end\": 566, \"text\": \"The chairman of the Party was Kemal Satır, an ex vice prime minister.\"}, \"D1S7\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d00\", \"start\": 567, \"end\": 570, \"text\": \"But\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 503, \"text\": \"Philadelphia ) : Willkie / McNary primaries 1944 ( Chicago ) : Dewey / Bricker primaries 1948 ( Philadelphia ) : Dewey / Warren primaries 1952 ( Chicago ) : Eisenhower / Nixon primaries 1956 ( San Francisco ) : Eisenhower / Nixon primaries 1960 ( Chicago ) : Nixon / Lodge primaries 1964 ( San Francisco ) : Goldwater / Miller primaries 1968 ( Miami Beach ) : Nixon / Agnew primaries 1972 ( Miami Beach ) : Nixon / Agnew primaries 1976 ( Kansas City ) : Ford / Dole primaries 1980 ( Detroit ) : Reagan /\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 450, \"text\": \"Party ( 1988–94 ) Greens Party ( YP ) ( 2008–12 ) Justice Party ( AP ) ( 1961–1980 ) Liberal Republican Party ( SCF ) ( 1995 ) Liberty Party ( HP ) ( 1955–58 ) Motherland Party ( ANAP ) ( 1983–2009 ) Nation Party ( MP ) ( 1948–53 ) Nation Party ( MP ) ( 1962–77 ) National Development Party ( MKP ) ( 1945–58 ) National Order Party ( MNP ) ( 1970–71 ) National Salvation Party ( MSP ) ( 1972–81 ) National Women's Party of Turkey ( TUKP ) ( 1972–81 )\"}, \"D4S1\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d03\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 120, \"text\": \"Republican Turkish Party The Republican Turkish Party (, CTP) is a social-democratic political party in Northern Cyprus.\"}, \"D4S2\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d03\", \"start\": 121, \"end\": 253, \"text\": \"The party was founded in 1970 by Ahmet Mithat Berberoğlu, a lawyer, in opposition to the leadership of Fazıl Küçük and Rauf Denktaş.\"}, \"D4S3\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d03\", \"start\": 254, \"end\": 441, \"text\": \"On 30 June 2008, the Republican Turkish Party became a consultative member of the Socialist International (voted in by all members except the Greek Cypriot Movement for Social Democracy).\"}, \"D4S4\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d03\", \"start\": 442, \"end\": 494, \"text\": \"It became a full member of the organization in 2014.\"}, \"D4S5\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d03\", \"start\": 495, \"end\": 599, \"text\": \"The CTP is a social democratic political party, positioned on the centre-left on the political spectrum.\"}, \"D4S6\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d03\", \"start\": 600, \"end\": 631, \"text\": \"The party espoused a pro-Soviet\"}, \"D5S1\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d04\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 61, \"text\": \"office , but was unable to pass major Square Deal proposals .\"}, \"D5S2\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d04\", \"start\": 62, \"end\": 209, \"text\": \"He did succeed in naming his successor , Secretary of War William Howard Taft , who easily defeated Bryan again in the 1908 presidential election .\"}, \"D5S3\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d04\", \"start\": 210, \"end\": 302, \"text\": \"[ 65 ] By 1907 , Roosevelt identified himself with the left-center of the Republican Party .\"}, \"D5S4\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d04\", \"start\": 303, \"end\": 534, \"text\": \"[ 66 ] He explained his balancing act : Again and again in my public career I have had to make head against mob spirit , against the tendency of poor , ignorant and turbulent people who feel a rancorous jealousy and hatred of those\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Republican Party\", \"scope\": \"Turkey\", \"claim\": \"The Republican Party was founded on 4 September 1972.\", \"answer\": \"4 September 1972\", \"quote\": \"Republican Party was founded by the second group in 1972. The party was founded on 4 September 1972.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d03\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d03:c0\", \"entity\": \"Republican Turkish Party\", \"scope\": \"founding date\", \"claim\": \"The Republican Turkish Party was founded in 1970.\", \"answer\": \"1970\", \"quote\": \"The party was founded in 1970 by Ahmet Mithat Berberoğlu, a lawyer, in opposition to the leadership of Fazıl Küçük and Rauf Denktaş.\", \"original_document_number\": 4}], \"R5_answers\": [\"4 September 1972\", \"1970\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"4 September 1972\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"1970\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C2\", \"answer\": \"1972\", \"origin\": \"proposal\"}], \"fallible_audits\": {\"J_A\": {\"audit\": {\"C0\": {\"fit\": \"direct\", \"support\": \"D1S5\", \"counter\": \"\", \"conflict\": \"uncertain\", \"observed_slot\": \"birth_date\", \"entity\": \"uncertain\", \"scope\": \"allowed\", \"constraint\": \"\"}, \"C1\": {\"fit\": \"wrong_argument\", \"support\": \"\", \"counter\": \"D4S2\", \"conflict\": \"same_referent\", \"observed_slot\": \"birth_date\", \"entity\": \"uncertain\", \"scope\": \"allowed\", \"constraint\": \"\"}, \"C2\": {\"fit\": \"incidental\", \"support\": \"D1S4\", \"counter\": \"\", \"conflict\": \"uncertain\", \"observed_slot\": \"birth_date\", \"entity\": \"uncertain\", \"scope\": \"allowed\", \"constraint\": \"\"}}}, \"J_B\": {\"audit\": {\"C0\": {\"fit\": \"direct\", \"support\": \"D1S5\", \"counter\": \"\", \"conflict\": \"uncertain\", \"observed_slot\": \"birth_date\", \"entity\": \"uncertain\", \"scope\": \"allowed\", \"constraint\": \"\"}, \"C1\": {\"fit\": \"wrong_argument\", \"support\": \"\", \"counter\": \"\", \"conflict\": \"uncertain\", \"observed_slot\": \"birth_date\", \"entity\": \"uncertain\", \"scope\": \"allowed\", \"constraint\": \"\"}, \"C2\": {\"fit\": \"incidental\", \"support\": \"D1S4\", \"counter\": \"\", \"conflict\": \"uncertain\", \"observed_slot\": \"birth_date\", \"entity\": \"uncertain\", \"scope\": \"allowed\", \"constraint\": \"\"}}}}}"
